  "title": "Who's Next",
  "country": "UK",
  "released": "1971-08-25",
  "notes": "This version has different labels to release [r487464]:\n- Labels have the side A tracklist in 3 lines and the side B tracklist in 2 lines, as opposed to 4 lines and 3 lines.\n- Also minor variations in text placing.\n\nSleeve printed and made by MacNeill Press Ltd., London, S.E.1\nMade In Gt.Britain\n\nSleeve has 'pleated' or 'pinched' spine endings: two pleats running for 1/2\" (12.5mm) from top down and bottom up.\n\nPlease note:\n- Vinyl with runouts \"variant 1, 4, 5, 6\" come with plain white poly-lined inner sleeve with \"0871\" date code (see photos).\n- Vinyl with runouts \"variant 2\" comes with plain white poly-lined inner sleeve with \"0771\" date code.\n- Vinyl with runouts \"variant 3, 7\" comes with plain white poly-lined inner sleeve with \"0571\" date code.\n\nIT IS VERY IMPORTANT TO NOTE:- that copies with the Head Hunters inner sleeve (see: [r7633337]) are re-pressings. Mainly for 2 reasons. Firstly the Head Hunters inner features LPs released 1 month later than this LP. And secondly this LP is already listed as 'available' on the inner - which means that this LP was already released when this Head Hunters inner sleeve was concieved. Therefore any copies with the Head Hunters inner sleeve will date from late September/October 1971 - at least 1 or 2 months after the release date. This inner DEFINITELY DID NOT EXIST at the time of this LPs release.\n\nRecorded and mixed at Olympic Studios, London.\nB4 recorded at Stargroves and mixed at Island Studios, London.\n\nPublished by Fabulous Music, except B4 published by Wistle Rhymes.\n\nMarketed by Polydor.\n\n℗ 1971\n\nCat# on labels: 2408 102\nCat# on spine: Deluxe 2408 102\nCat# on back cover: 2408 102 Deluxe\n\nRunouts are stamped, except for the upside down etching 'MG 12888' on side A.",
  "released_formatted": "25 Aug 1971",
